    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\nThe change is confined to a single small, cohesive function class:\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds `customerCode` as `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n- `CITY3` / `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of city / last name (shared `prefix` helper).\n- `NNNN` = per-city sequence, one more than the owners already in that city (filtered `findAll()` count, since this runs before `SaveOwner`).\n\n**Membership number** required no edit: `OwnerMapper` derives it as `owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M...\"`, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 as does anything else built from `customerCode`.\n\nStructural impact stayed low: one file touched, one method changed. The two new `private static` helpers keep the changed `service` method simple (its own CC stays 1) and the class's `WMC_other` minimal, rather than growing one complex method.",
